    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 9,
      "text": "Heard learned counsel for the petitioner and learned Public Prosecutor.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 1039,
      "end": 1110,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 10,
      "text": "Perused the material available on record.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 1111,
      "end": 1152,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 11,
      "text": "As per the prosecution, the victim- 'R' aged about 7 years was subjected to forcible sexual assault- rape by the petitioner who was working as Gateman of the school where she is studying.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 1153,
      "end": 1341,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 12,
      "text": "This Court, after perusing the challan papers, Medico-legal Examination Report of Sexual Offence dated 14.07.2023 prepared [2025:RJ-JD:1662] (2 of 2) [CRLMB-8150/2024] at Department of Forensic Medicine and Toxicology, Dr. S.N. Medical College, Jodhpur so also the statements of the Ashok vs State Of Rajasthan (2025:Rj-Jd:1662) on 10 January, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/18444759/\n1 victim- 'R' recorded under Section 164 Cr.P.C. and the statements of various witnesses including the statements of Dr. Asmita (PW.7) recorded before the competent criminal Court, finds that there is prima facie evidence available on record against the petitioner that he committed sexual assault- rape on the victim- 'R'.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 1342,
      "end": 2069,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "14.07.2023",
          "label": "DATE",
          "start": 1446,
          "end": 1456
        },
        {
          "text": "Department of Forensic Medicine and Toxicology, Dr. S.N. Medical College, Jodhpur",
          "label": "ORG",
          "start": 1514,
          "end": 1595
        },
        {
          "text": "Ashok vs State Of Rajasthan",
          "label": "PRECEDENT",
          "start": 1626,
          "end": 1653
        },
        {
          "text": "Section 164",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 1775,
          "end": 1786
        },
        {
          "text": "Cr.P.C.",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 1787,
          "end": 1794
        },
        {
          "text": "Asmita",
          "label": "WITNESS",
          "start": 1867,
          "end": 1873
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 13,
      "text": "Further, considering the fact that the victim- 'R' is a girl of seven years, who was allegedly subjected to rape, the gravity of the offence is obvious.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 2070,
      "end": 2222,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 14,
      "text": "This Court while dealing with the bail applications in such matters cannot be oblivious of the fact that an offence like rape devastates the victim for the rest of her life.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 2223,
      "end": 2396,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 15,
      "text": "Hence, this criminal bail application is devoid of any merit and is, hereby, dismissed.\n(KULDEEP MATHUR),J 9-divya/-\nPowered by TCPDF (www.tcpdf.org)\nAshok vs State Of Rajasthan (2025:Rj-Jd:1662) on 10 January, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/18444759/\n2",
